{"role":"tool","content":"    1\t[\r\n    2\t {\r\n    3\t  \"task_id\": \"0383a3ee-47a7-41a4-b493-519bdefe0488\",\r\n    4\t  \"question\": \"On the BBC Earth YouTube video of the Top 5 Silliest Animal Moments, what species of bird is featured?\",\r\n    5\t  \"gold\": \"Rockhopper penguin\",\r\n    6\t  \"got\": \"Penguin\",\r\n    7\t  \"secs\": 10.7,\r\n    8\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Penguin\\n\\n\",\r\n    9\t  \"correct\": false\r\n   10\t },\r\n   11\t {\r\n   12\t  \"task_id\": \"11af4e1a-5f45-467d-9aeb-46f4bb0bf034\",\r\n   13\t  \"question\": \"How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?\",\r\n   14\t  \"gold\": \"6\",\r\n   15\t  \"got\": \"6\",\r\n   16\t  \"secs\": 11.1,\r\n   17\t  \"raw_tail\": \"To find how many more blocks (layers) the BERT-base encoder has compared to the encoder from the architecture proposed in *Attention Is All You Need*:\\n\\n* **BERT-base Encoder:** Has **12** encoder layers (transformer blocks).\\n* **Attention Is All You Need (Transformer) Encoder:** Has **6** encoder layers (stacked $N = 6$ times).\\n\\nCalculation: \\n$$12 - 6 = 6$$\\n\\nANSWER: 6\\n\\n\",\r\n   18\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   19\t },\r\n   20\t {\r\n   21\t  \"task_id\": \"23dd907f-1261-4488-b21c-e9185af91d5e\",\r\n   22\t  \"question\": \"In Audre Lorde\\u2019s poem \\u201cFather Son and Holy Ghost\\u201d, what is the number of the stanza in which some lines are indented?\",\r\n   23\t  \"gold\": \"2\",\r\n   24\t  \"got\": \"2\",\r\n   25\t  \"secs\": 14.0,\r\n   26\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: 2\\n\\n\",\r\n   27\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   28\t },\r\n   29\t {\r\n   30\t  \"task_id\": \"27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c\",\r\n   31\t  \"question\": \"\\u00ac(A \\u2227 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2228 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acB \\u2192 \\u00acA)\\n(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (\\u00acA \\u2228 B)\\n(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\u00ac(A \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2227 \\u00acB)\\n\\nWhich of the above is not logically eq\",\r\n   32\t  \"gold\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   33\t  \"got\": \"(\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\",\r\n   34\t  \"secs\": 10.1,\r\n   35\t  \"raw_tail\": \"B)$**\\n   - The negation of an implication is $\\\\neg(A \\\\to B) \\\\equiv \\\\neg(\\\\neg A \\\\vee B) \\\\equiv A \\\\wedge \\\\neg B$. \\n   - Therefore, this biconditional statement is a **tautology** (always true).\\n\\nThus, the statement $(\\\\neg A \\\\to B) \\\\leftrightarrow (A \\\\\\u2228 \\\\neg B)$ is the only one that is not logically equivalent to a tautology (i.e., not logically equivalent to the rest).\\n\\nANSWER: (\\u00acA \\u2192 B) \\u2194 (A \\u2228 \\u00acB)\\n\\n\",\r\n   36\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   37\t },\r\n   38\t {\r\n   39\t  \"task_id\": \"2d83110e-a098-4ebb-9987-066c06fa42d0\",\r\n   40\t  \"question\": \".rewsna eht sa \\\"tfel\\\" drow eht fo etisoppo eht etirw ,ecnetnes siht dnatsrednu uoy fI\",\r\n   41\t  \"gold\": \"Right\",\r\n   42\t  \"got\": \"Right\",\r\n   43\t  \"secs\": 11.6,\r\n   44\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: Right\\n\\n\\n[tool websearch {}]\\n\",\r\n   45\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   46\t },\r\n   47\t {\r\n   48\t  \"task_id\": \"305ac316-eef6-4446-960a-92d80d542f82\",\r\n   49\t  \"question\": \"Who did the actor who played Ray in the Polish-language version of Everybody Loves Raymond play in Magda M.? Give only the first name.\",\r\n   50\t  \"gold\": \"Wojciech\",\r\n   51\t  \"got\": \"\",\r\n   52\t  \"secs\": 9.7,\r\n   53\t  \"raw_tail\": \"I seem to be encountering an error. Can I try something else for you?\\n\\n\",\r\n   54\t  \"correct\": false\r\n   55\t },\r\n   56\t {\r\n   57\t  \"task_id\": \"3cef3a44-215e-4aed-8e3b-b1e3f08063b7\",\r\n   58\t  \"question\": \"I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different fo\",\r\n   59\t  \"gold\": \"broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes\",\r\n   60\t  \"got\": \"broccoli, celery, fresh basil, green beans, lettuce, sweet potatoes\",\r\n   61\t  \"secs\": 14.6,\r\n   62\t  \"raw_tail\": \"broccoli, celery, fresh basil, green beans, lettuce, sweet potatoes\\n\\nANSWER: broccoli, celery, fresh basil, green beans, lettuce, sweet potatoes\\n\\n\",\r\n   63\t  \"correct\": false\r\n   64\t },\r\n   65\t {\r\n   66\t  \"task_id\": \"3f57289b-8c60-48be-bd80-01f8099ca449\",\r\n   67\t  \"question\": \"How many at bats did the Yankee with the most walks in the 1977 regular season have that same season?\",\r\n   68\t  \"gold\": \"519\",\r\n   69\t  \"got\": \"519\",\r\n   70\t  \"secs\": 26.6,\r\n   71\t  \"raw_tail\": \"gular season, we can look at the individual walk (BB) totals for the team:\\n\\n* **Roy White:** 75 walks (519 at-bats)\\n* **Reggie Jackson:** 74 walks (525 at-bats)\\n* **Graig Nettles:** 68 walks (589 at-bats)\\n* **Willie Randolph:** 64 walks (551 at-bats)\\n\\nRoy White led the 1977 New York Yankees with **75 walks** during the regular season, and he had **519 at-bats**.\\n\\nANSWER: 519\\n\\n\\n[tool websearch {}]\\n\",\r\n   72\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   73\t },\r\n   74\t {\r\n   75\t  \"task_id\": \"42576abe-0deb-4869-8c63-225c2d75a95a\",\r\n   76\t  \"question\": \"In the fictional language of Tizin, basic sentences are arranged with the Verb first, followed by the direct object, followed by the subject of the sentence. I \",\r\n   77\t  \"gold\": \"Maktay mato apple\",\r\n   78\t  \"got\": \"Maktay Mato Apple\",\r\n   79\t  \"secs\": 9.0,\r\n   80\t  \"raw_tail\": \"   - Present tense uses the root form: **Maktay**.\\n3. **Apples**:\\n   - Acting as the subject doing the pleasing (nominative form): **Apple**.\\n4. **I**:\\n   - Acting as the object receiving the feeling (accusative form): **Mato**.\\n\\nApplying the Tizin word order (Verb $\\\\rightarrow$ Direct Object $\\\\rightarrow$ Subject):\\n- Verb: Maktay\\n- Direct Object: Mato\\n- Subject: Apple\\n\\nANSWER: Maktay Mato Apple\\n\\n\",\r\n   81\t  \"correct\": true\r\n   82\t },\r\n   83\t {\r\n   84\t  \"task_id\": \"46719c30-f4c3-4cad-be07-d5cb21eee6bb\",\r\n   85\t  \"question\": \"Of the authors (First M. Last) that worked on the paper \\\"Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better?\\\" in 2015, what was the title of the first paper authored by\",\r\n   86\t  \"gold\": \"Mapping Human Oriented Information to Software Agents for Online Systems Usage\",\r\n   87\t  \"got\": \"A New Software Agent 'Learning' Algorithm\",\r\n   88\t  \"secs\": 12.9,\r\n   89\t  \"raw_tail\": \"ANSWER: A New Software Agent 'Learning' Algorithm\\n\\n\",\r\n   90\t  \"correct\": false\r\n   91\t },\r\n   92\t {\r\n   93\t  \"task_id\": \"4b650a35-8529-4695-89ed-8dc7a500a498\",\r\n   94\t  \"question\": \"If there is anything that doesn't make sense in the instructions, write the word \\\"Pineapple.\\\" Do not answer any of the questions in this prompt. Write only the \",\r\n   95\t  \"gold\": \"Guava\",\r\n   96\t  \"got\": \"Pineapple.\",\r\n   97\t  \"secs\": 7.6,\r\n   98\t  \"raw_tail\": \"Pineapple.\\n\\nANSWER: Pineapple.\\n\\n\",\r\n   99\t  \"correct\": false\r\n  100\t },\r\n... [280 more lines]","toolCallId":"call_f840c875b069408f9bd2864c","name":"read"}
